load @/code/type/term
  find term

load @/code/type/multiplicity
  find multiplicity

# The dependent function type, the pi type, the one way the theory forms a type that depends on a value. A pi type
# gathers a domain type, a multiplicity saying how the argument may be used, and a codomain type that may mention the
# argument. An ordinary function is the special case where the codomain ignores the argument. The multiplicity on the
# domain is what makes this a quantitative theory: an erased argument is a type or proof present only for checking, a
# linear argument is used exactly once, a shared argument any number of times. The universe a pi inhabits is the
# maximum of its domain's and codomain's, except at the impredicative bottom, where a pi landing in Type 0 stays in
# Type 0 whatever the domain.
#
# The rules. Introduction: a lambda inhabits a pi type when, given an argument of the domain, its body inhabits the
# codomain. Elimination: applying a function of a pi type to an argument of the domain yields the codomain at that
# argument. Computation (beta): applying a lambda to an argument substitutes the argument into the body, the engine of
# normalization.
form function-type
  link domain, like term
  link usage, like multiplicity
  link codomain, like term
